DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("((x^2))^(1/2)");
$fun_1 = Formula("(x-3)^2");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_4 = Compute("{-7, 10} - ((-infinity, infinity) - (8, infinity)) - ((-infinity, infinity) - (8, infinity))");
$set_ans_5 = Compute("((8, infinity) - ({-7, 10} U (8, infinity)))");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("({-7, -4, 0, 1, 2} U (-infinity, 13) U (({-7, -4, -3, 1, 5, 6}))) U (-infinity, 13)");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("{-7, -4, -3, 1, 5, 6} - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-7, -4, -3, 1, 5, 6}) - ((-infinity, infinity) - (-infinity, 13))");
$set_ans_3 = Compute("{-7, -4, 0, 1, 2} U ((({-7, -4, 0, 1, 2})) - ((-infinity, infinity) - ((-infinity, 13)))) U {-7, -4, -3, 1, 5, 6} U {-7, -4, -3, 1, 5, 6}");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

- _For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._
- _For derivative problems, if the result is undefined, then *leave the blank empty*._

What is the value of [`1+6/16`]? [_____]{answer=>Formula('1.375'),width=>9}
---

[`7/19+10/17`] is equal to [_____]{Formula('0.956656346749')}
---

What is the value of [`6+14+9+5*2`]? [_____]{Real(39.)}
---

[`12/5+5`] is equal to [_____]{answer=>Real(7.4),width=>5}
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | x < 13\}`]
- [`B = \{-7, -4, -3, 1, 5, 6\}`]
- [`C = \{-7, -4, 0, 1, 2\}`]

Compute:
- [`(C \cup A \cup ((B))) \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`B \cap B \cap A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}
- [`C \cup (((C)) \cap (A)) \cup B \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | x > 7\}`]
- [`B = \{-7, 10\}`]
- [`C = \{-4, 5, 10\}`]

Compute:
- [`B \cap A \cap A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}
- [`A - (B \cup A) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_5}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -6, 8, -8 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -3, -2, 0 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle 10, -2, 9 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \left\| \vec{u} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-6, 8, -8>"))}
- [` \vec{v} \cdot \vec{w} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-3, -2, 0>") . Compute("<10, -2, 9>")}
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-3, -2, 0>") x Compute("<-6, 8, -8>")}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-3, -2, 0>"))}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{Compute("<10, -2, 9>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -9, 3, 3 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 5, -10, 0 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle 10, 8, -7 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \left\| \vec{w} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<10, 8, -7>"))}
- [` \left\| \vec{v} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<5, -10, 0>"))}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<5, -10, 0>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{Compute("<10, 8, -7>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- [` \vec{w} \times \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<10, 8, -7>") x Compute("<5, -10, 0>")}
- [` \vec{w} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<10, 8, -7>") x Compute("<-9, 3, 3>")}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->D()}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->D()}
- [`f'(9) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>9)}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
